<header><p class="st-kicker">protectorate · Horn and East Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">British Somaliland</h1><p class="st-meta">1884 CE – 1960 CE · capital Berbera; later Hargeisa</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A British protectorate on the Gulf of Aden coast of Somalia, which fought a 20-year war with the Dervishes and became independent as Somaliland in 1960.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain's</a> interest in the northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somalis">Somali</a> coast came from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aden">Aden</a>, which depended on Somali livestock. Between 1884 and 1886 British officers signed treaties with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/isaaq-sultanate">Isaaq</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gadabuursi">Gadabuursi</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/warsangali-sultanate">Warsangali</a> and other clans, and after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> withdrew from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zeila">Zeila</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbera">Berbera</a> the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a> was established, run at first from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/british-raj">British India</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>British rule was thin and cheap, aimed at keeping the coast secure and the meat trade flowing. From 1899 the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/dervish-state">Dervish State</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mohammed-abdullah-hassan">Mohammed Abdullah Hassan</a> fought a long war against the British, ended in 1920 by a campaign that used aircraft. Pastoral clans kept their customary institutions under appointed elders and Islamic courts. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> occupied the territory briefly in 1940 to 1941.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>On 26 June 1960 British <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/state-of-somaliland">Somaliland</a> became independent as the State of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-somaliland">Somaliland</a>, which five days later united with the former <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/trust-territory-of-somaliland">Trust Territory of Somaliland</a> to form the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/somali-republic">Somali Republic</a>. Its borders were revived by the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-somaliland">Republic of Somaliland</a> in 1991.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/british-somaliland.jpg" alt="British Somaliland" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: Sodacan · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_British_Somaliland_(1903%E2%80%931950).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1884 CE – 1960 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>protectorate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Berbera; later Hargeisa</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Somali, English</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/somalia">Somalia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Somaliland Protectorate</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1922&amp;focus=british-somaliland" aria-label="British Somaliland on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5920 1788 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where British Somaliland lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6240 2044L6327 2016M6240 2044L6216 2076M6240 2044L6337 2092M6240 2044L4997 651M6240 2044L6070 2096M6240 2044L6216 2076"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6327 2016h0M6216 2076h0M6337 2092h0M4997 651h0M6070 2096h0M6216 2076h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6240 2044h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6240 2044h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Berbera. <a href="/atlas?year=1922&amp;focus=british-somaliland">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
